<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Province Wellesley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1800</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Seberang Perai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Province Wellesley, now Seberang Perai, is the mainland part of the Malaysian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penang">Penang</a>, a strip of coast facing Penang island. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Kedah ceded it to the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in 1800, and it was named after Richard Wellesley, governor-general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It gave the colony control of the coast opposite George Town and later formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/straits-settlements">Straits Settlements</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/province-wellesley.jpg" alt="Province Wellesley" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HundenvonPenang · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skyline_of_Butterworth_in_Seberang_Perai_2025.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
